      "cell": "NOT SIGNIFICANT",
      "gloss": {
       "ar": "\u063a\u064a\u0631 \u062f\u0627\u0644 \u0625\u062d\u0635\u0627\u0626\u064a\u0627\u064b\u060c \u0645\u0639 \u0648\u0643\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0628\u0645\u064a\u0632\u0627\u0646\u064a\u0629 C1",
       "en": "Not statistically significant, with agents at the C1 budget"
      }
     },
     {
      "cell": "INCONCLUSIVE (post-hoc)",
      "gloss": {
       "ar": "\u063a\u064a\u0631 \u062d\u0627\u0633\u0645\u060c \u0648\u0647\u064a \u0642\u0631\u0627\u0621\u0629 \u0644\u0627\u062d\u0642\u0629: \u0627\u0644\u062d\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0623\u062f\u0646\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0645 (50 \u0648\u062d\u062f\u0629) \u062d\u064f\u062f\u0650\u0651\u062f \u0628\u0639\u062f \u0623\u0646 \u0639\u064f\u0631\u0641\u062a \u0646\u062a\u064a\u062c\u0629 Phase D\u060c \u0641\u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0635\u0646\u064a\u0641 \u0644\u0645 \u064a\u064f\u0633\u062c\u064e\u0651\u0644 \u0645\u0633\u0628\u0642\u0627\u064b. \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062c\u0631\u0628\u0629 \u0644\u0627 \u062a\u0645\u064a\u0651\u0632 \u0628\u064a\u0646 \"\u0644\u0627 \u0623\u062b\u0631\" \u0648\"\u0623\u062b\u0631 \u064a\u0647\u0645\u0651 \u0627\u0644\u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642\"",
       "en": "Inconclusive, and a post-hoc reading: the MEI (50 units) was set after Phase D's result was known, so this classification was not preregistered. The experiment cannot tell \"no effect\" from \"an effect the team cares about\""
      }
     }
    ],
    "lines": [
     {
      "file": "PHASE_D_RESULT.txt",
      "key": "result",
      "line": 26,
      "text": "  RESULT: NOT SIGNIFICANT at alpha 0.05.\n  These are C1 agents: 50 000 steps, 11 training episodes each,\n  which train.py itself calls 'the first bad run'. So the claim\n  is 'with agents trained to the C1 budget, preview does not\n  separate from seed noise' -- NOT 'preview does not help'.\n  See results/PREREGISTRATION.md limit 6."
     },
     {
      "file": "PHASE_D_RESULT.txt",
      "key": "not_blind",
      "line": 33,
      "text": "  AND THE BLINDED ARM IS NOT BLIND. The road is the same hill at\n  the same second in every episode, and the blind agent's thermal\n  state takes a distinct value at every step -- a clock on a road\n  it can memorise. So this compares an explicit preview channel\n  with an implicit one, not foresight with none. Four explanations\n  for the null are live and this experiment separates none of them.\n  Randomise the climb per episode before reading anything into it.\n  See results/PREREGISTRATION.md limits 7 and 8."
     },
     {
      "file": "PHASE_D2_RESULT.txt",
      "key": "post_hoc",
      "line": 65,
      "text": "  RESULT: INCONCLUSIVE   [MEI set AFTER this result -- see below]\n  This experiment cannot tell 'no effect' from 'an effect the team\n  would care about'. It is a statement about the experiment's\n  size, not a statement that preview does nothing.\n  power_analysis.py explains it -- but was written after this\n  result, so it is an explanation, not a prediction.\n\n  Phase D's primary test is unaffected: its verdict was 'not\n  significant' and still is. The MEI was set on 22 September,\n  AFTER Phase D's result was known, so Phase D's classification\n  under the MEI rule is a POST-HOC reading and is labelled so.\n  results/PREREGISTRATION.md section 5 records the ordering."
     }
    ],
